  "privacyIntro": "MoneyLedger is an expense-sharing app without a central server. It has no account system of its own — you sign in with your Matrix account — shows no ads, contains no analytics or tracking, and does not sell or share your data. MoneyLedger is published by Leo Stumpf, an individual developer. There is no MoneyLedger server that could receive your data.",
  "privacyLedgerTitle": "Your ledger stays on your devices",
  "privacyLedgerBody": "Groups, participants, expenses and payments are stored only in a local database on each device signed in to a member's account. Every member of a group has a copy of that group's ledger — that is how sharing works: the names, Matrix IDs, expenses and payments in a group are visible to all of its members.",
  "privacyHomeserverTitle": "What your Matrix homeserver sees",
  "privacyHomeserverBody": "To sync, MoneyLedger sends every change as an end-to-end-encrypted Matrix to-device message to the other members' devices. Your homeserver (and the homeservers of the other members) relay these messages and queue them until they are delivered, but cannot read them. They do see metadata: which accounts and devices exchange messages, when, how often and roughly how large they are. Your Matrix account itself — user name, devices, encryption keys, IP addresses and sign-in history — is handled by your homeserver under its own privacy policy.",
  "privacyNoTrackingTitle": "No analytics, no servers of ours",
  "privacyNoTrackingBody": "The app only talks to your homeserver — and, if you use single sign-on or sign up on the web, to the pages your homeserver sends you to in your browser. There is no analytics, no crash reporting, no advertising ID and no tracking of any kind.",
  "privacyBackgroundTitle": "Background sync on Android",
  "privacyBackgroundBody": "On Android, MoneyLedger can sync about every 15 minutes while the app is closed (only with a network connection and not on low battery). It uses the same encrypted messages to your homeserver and shows no notifications. You can turn it off in Settings. The web version syncs only while its tab is open.",
  "privacyCsvTitle": "CSV export and import",
  "privacyCsvBody": "Exporting a group writes a CSV file with its expenses, the participants' names and the amounts — only when you ask for it. Where that file goes is your choice; it is not encrypted, and MoneyLedger has no visibility into it afterwards. Importing reads only the file you pick.",
  "privacyBackupTitle": "Device backups",
  "privacyBackupBody": "Android's automatic app backup is not switched off. If backup is enabled on your phone, the app's local data (your ledger and your Matrix session) may be included in your device backup to your Google account, under Android's backup rules.",
  "privacyDeleteTitle": "Deleting your data",
  "privacyDeleteBody": "• Leave or delete a group (group menu ⋮): it and all its records are removed from this device. When you leave, the other members are told that you left.\n• Signing out keeps this account's ledger on the device, so it is back when you sign in again.\n• Uninstalling the app (or clearing its storage) removes everything it stored on the device.\n• Copies on other members' devices are theirs: they keep the group's history, including your expenses in it.\n• Your Matrix account can be deactivated through your homeserver.",
  "privacyContactTitle": "Contact",
  "privacyContactBody": "Questions, or anything that looks wrong here: open an issue at https://github.com/LeoStumpf/MoneyLedger or email leo.m.stumpf@gmail.com."
}
